{"n": 1065, "w": 1000, "h": 764, "img": "1065.webp", "text": "Condition\n\nRattling noise\n\nSun roof can be lifted, but does not slide\n\nSun roof lifts onesidedly\n\nGrinding noise when opening and closing\nGrinding noise when lifting\n\nWater leaking through roof liner area\n\n54-9\n\nTROUBLESHOOTING SUN ROOF\n\nab Maladjusted\n\nb) Guide tubes knocking against each other\n\nc) Roof liner frame knocking against sun roof hid\nwhen open\n\nd) Connector for water drain knocking on guide rail\n\ne) Excessive play of slides in guide rails as well as upper\n\nQuide pins in gates\n\n3) Pins on gate holders bent ~\n\na) Drive cables maladjusted in position 0\n\nb) Rear guide turns on drive cable\n\n@) Sliding rails and plastic parts lubricated\n\nFront seal dry\n\nContact force on front seal excessive\n\n8) Sun roof maladjusted in position 0\nb) Seals loose/damaged\n\n¢) Wrong seal installed (front/rear seals different in shape)\n\nd) Drain hoses plugged\n\ne) Guide rails and cover plates seal insufficiently on\nroof frame\n\nft) Corners in rear roof opening leak\ng) Hose outlets plugged with sealing compound foam\n\nCorrection\n\na)\nb)\n\nc\n\nd)\n\na)\na)\n\nb)\n\na)\na)\nb)\na)\nb)\nc)\nd)\n\nAdjust sun root\nWrap tape around guide tubes\n\nPaste foam rubber on corners of sun roof frame\n\nPaste tape on rivets and guide linkage\nSee Service Information 54 01 84 (298)\n\nReplace gate holders\nAdjust drive cables in position 0\n\nLock drive cable im front of and behind guide with\npunch marks or by squeezing\n\nRemove grease and/or replace slides\nLubricate seal with vaseline\n\nAdjust lid\n\nAdjust sun roof in position 0\nPaste/replace seals\n\nInstall original spare parts\n\nClean drain hoses\n\nSeal guide rails and cover plates\n\nSeal corners\n\nClean hoses", "words": [["Condition", 0.0441, 0.1326, 0.0917, 0.1439], ["Rattling", 0.0446, 0.1645, 0.0836, 0.1784], ["noise", 0.0866, 0.1678, 0.1099, 0.1757], ["Sun", 0.0446, 0.3574, 0.0633, 0.3687], ["roof", 0.0669, 0.357